      "id": "N20V7-F10",
      "severity": "critical",
      "summary": "A sixth live-verified defect found by N70's real production unit run -- and a correction of a mistaken diagnosis (N20V7-F09, attempts 6) made earlier in this same lineage against a stale/incomplete checkpoint read. Live rerun of N70 with N20V7-F09's fix in place progressed further (now genuinely entering D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS from D91's repair destination -- proof the routing concern F09 targeted was never actually broken: D91's own outgoing edge is `routing.route_model_failure`, which reads `pending_guard` directly and never consults `pending_failure` or the generic `_failure_destination` hijack path at all) but then failed inside D17 itself: 'D17 was routed with an empty or missing findings list'. Root cause, confirmed via direct SQLite checkpoint archaeology of this exact live run (`outputs/run27/live_unit`, run_id `1f279267aabb080ca4cf58293303f2915e6f2f9eab0bb79eadfb48a6d19e3c5b`): `D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS` (repair.py) has two entry branches -- one reads a classified `pending_failure` (`classification == 'repair'`) that D91 leaves in place specifically for D17 to build its one raw finding from, then D17 clears it itself once consumed; the other reads `pending_guard.detail.findings` for D08/D09/D12/D14/D16-sourced repairs. N20V7-F09's fix nulled `pending_failure` inside D91 for the 'repair' decision, which starved D17 of the only data it had to work with the moment a real M01 discovery sub-request failed content policy (`candidate_undeclared_artifact`, safety_focus:002, 'discovery must emit locators, not interpretations') and D91 routed it to D17 for repair. Fixed within N20's write set (runtime/langgraph_factory/model_nodes.py): D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE reverted to clearing `pending_failure` only on the 'retry' decision -- the original, correct behavior. The prior regression test asserting the wrong (F09) behavior was replaced with an integration-style test that drives D91 then repair.D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS directly against a real M01 discovery-failure shape, proving the classified pending_failure survives to D17, D17 builds a real finding_partitions entry from it, D17 clears pending_failure itself, and D17's own subsequent routing correctly resolves to D18_PLAN_TARGETED_UNIT_REPAIR. Full 8-file N20 suite: 475 passed, 1 skipped, 140 subtests passed. Zero scan violations."
    }
